; qwen38-heed-cost-probe.fk — the controlled run that separates CONTEXT LENGTH
; from INJECTION as the driver of per-position cost.
;
; The grounded run walked 506 positions and the bare run 75, and the CPU-side
; (non-GPU) cost per position differed fivefold. Two explanations fit: the
; injected span is expensive per se, or per-position cost simply grows with how
; much context is already there.
;
; This run walks a long way with NO envelope and NO injection at all. If the
; CPU-side per-position cost rises anyway, the driver is context length and the
; interpreter is the thing that scales badly. If it stays flat, injection is.
;
; Effectful: opens a sealed 29GB GGUF and drives the GPU. Do not preflight.
; preludes: form/form-stdlib/form-cli-model-generate.fk

(fcmg-heed-witness
    "/Users/ursmuff/models/qwen38-27b/Qwen3.8-27B-Q8_0.gguf"
    "Count slowly from one to one hundred. Write one number per line, nothing else."
    420
    8)
